=== ADDENDUM 12:28 (written BEFORE any re-run) -- env reconciliation + instrument incident
The first cross-box attempt (12:19) is VOID. All six child runs (X1 n=3, X3 n=3) crashed at startup in ~1.7s with
  zakcode.providers.endpoints.LocalOnlyViolation
because zc-01's user config (~/.zakcode -> /etc/zakcode/.env) sets ZAKCODE_LOCAL_ONLY, which the zc-03 reference
runs never saw (zc-03 has no ~/.zakcode/.env; its process env is exactly OPENAI_API_KEY + OPENAI_BASE_URL +
ZAKCODE_ZAKPICK_MODELS + ZAKCODE_TEMPERATURE + ZBENCH_*). The arm nonetheless printed
  "PRIMARY (every file): IDENTICAL across all runs"
over the UNTOUCHED seed files (digest 1bb446844e2f, files=2, verify_rc=1, turns=None) -- guard-2903 class, one
level above the empty-digest refusal shipped this morning. Crashed JSONs archived at zc-01:/root/zb-vacuous/.
Instrument fix (branch det-noreport-refusal): determinism_arm.py records no_report per run and refuses (rc=5)
when any run produced no report; a report with success=false still counts as a measurement.
Reconciliation rule, decided now: the bench child on zc-01 runs with ZAKCODE_HOME=/root/zbench-home (an EMPTY
dir), so no user .env is loaded and the process env has the local shape. The pod ignores the bearer token
(/models and chat/completions both HTTP 200 without auth), so the differing placeholder keys cannot reach the model.
X1/X2/X3 decision rules unchanged. Reference digests unchanged: 7bff3055078d.

